From 52868898a47e7fbec264e6b22a37b5f621a7846a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 22:36:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui): queue typed prompts behind gateway background
 turns; prompt wake after holds

Three hub findings from 2026-11-21 (core d912ee96dd38), plus one Desktop tagging fix:

1. Typing into a chat held by the gateway's own Kanban notice / close-out turn no
   longer takes it over (which killed that turn with session_turn_lease_lost: chats
   39be4c, 8d8534, a30b). When the only other holder (durable turn lease and registry
   leases) is the live default gateway and the newest turn is automated, prompt.submit
   forwards the prompt into that gateway's FIFO (RT-37 owner_forward) and answers the
   queued, forwarded receipt the Desktop already renders as a queued row. Any other
   holder, an unforwardable message or a forward that queued nothing keeps auto take-over;
   an unconfirmed forward is never taken over. A Stop gesture on such a chat takes it
   over (session.take_over on a worker thread), which ends the background turn.
2. A notice wake refused only by the core update's admission hold charges no attempt,
   is stamped closeout.hold_wait, is due (no grace) the moment the hold lifts, and a
   watcher (notice_hold_wait) runs the guarantee pass within 2 s of the lift, then every
   5 s while wakes wait for a slot (wake slots bound the rate). The sweep's passive rows
   for such wakes carry the same stamp; other busy refusals keep their backoff.
3. A retiring backend (host_loop_lease.retire_host_loops: code skew, superseded) now
   publishes run/host-loops/retiring/<pid>.json. A wake refused "has another live owner"
   whose every other holder is retiring re-claims the slot each 1 s for 15 s, then
   answers busy (transient) instead of refused. The slot claim stays the only way in.
4. Desktop: primary-socket events are tagged with the primary's own connection id
   (store/gateway-primary-socket.ts), not the foregrounded secondary's, so plugins
   filtering by connectionId stop attributing primary pushes to e.g. hermes-hub.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
